<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">College of William &amp; Mary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1693">1693</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as College of William and Mary</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The College of William &amp; Mary is a public university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/williamsburg-virginia">Williamsburg, Virginia</a>, founded by royal charter in 1693 under King William III and Queen Mary II. It is the second-oldest institution of higher education in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, after Harvard. Its students included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-monroe">James Monroe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-marshall">John Marshall</a>, and the Phi Beta Kappa society was founded there in 1776.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Church of England was established, and the <b>College of William and Mary</b> was founded in 1693.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-virginia">Colony of Virginia</a></li></ul></section>
